course: dictionary
lesson: 6269
title: Days of the week: Monday
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Monday is the day of the week after Sunday and before Tuesday. For many children it is the first school day of the week. To check a day, ask yourself which day comes just before it and which comes just after.
explain: When you see «on Mondays», the words mean every Monday, not just one Monday. If a club meets «on Mondays», you can go every single week on that day.
explain: In a story, the days are clues to when things happen. «Nine-year-old Ella Brown rescued six ducklings from a drain on Monday.» The word Monday tells you the day the rescue happened.
explain: A week has 7 days, so the Monday after this one comes 7 days later. Count the days on your fingers if you are not sure. This helps with maths problems too.
fact: Monday is the day of the week after Sunday and before Tuesday.
fact: Number the days of the week: Monday is 1, Tuesday 2, and Sunday 7.
fact: «On Mondays» means every Monday.
fact: Monday is a noun, and its plural is Mondays.
fact: In Chinese, Monday is «xīngqīyī», which you can say as «shing-chee-YEE».
exercise: «Nine-year-old Ella Brown rescued six ducklings from a drain on Monday.» What day was the rescue? | Sunday | Friday | Tuesday | *Monday
exercise: If today is Sunday, what day is tomorrow? | Saturday | Tuesday | *Monday | Friday
exercise: Which day comes just before Monday? | Tuesday | *Sunday | Saturday | Friday
test: A swimming club meets «on Mondays». How often does it meet? | Only on Tuesdays | *Every Monday | Once a year | Only once in a while
test: Monday is day 1 of the week. Which number is Sunday? | 8 | *7 | 1 | 6
exam: If today is Monday, which day will it be exactly 7 days later? | *Monday | Sunday | Tuesday | Wednesday
